# Every text file is checked out with LF line endings, on every system.
#
# The gate compares files byte for byte: generated sources and pages against
# what the catalog compiles to, golden outputs, the kernel's copy of the plugin
# world against its digest. A checkout that rewrote line endings to CRLF on
# Windows would make every one of those comparisons fail on a tree that is
# right. No file here is binary, so nothing needs to be marked `-text`.
* text=auto eol=lf
